      "exampleArabic": "مع السلامة",
      "exampleTransliteration": "maʿa s-salāmati",
      "exampleEnglish": "Goodbye (lit. 'with safety').",
      "grammarNote": "Three fixed expressions, each treated as one phrase-vocabulary entry the same way السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ was in level 1 — not meant to be grammatically decomposed. مَعَ السَّلَامَةِ is level 1's greeting's natural counterpart: hello and goodbye, finally bookending the course. إِنْ شَاءَ اللَّه ('God willing') is one of the most common phrases in everyday Arabic, used whenever discussing future plans. أَهْلًا وَسَهْلًا ('welcome') is what you'll hear entering almost any home, shop, or event.",
